.TH mbphotogrammetry 1 "7 September 2026" "MB-System 5.0" "MB-System 5.0"
.SH NAME
\fBmbphotogrammetry\fP \- Generate bathymetry soundings from navigated stereo pairs of downlooking seafloor photographs.

.SH VERSION
Version 5.0

.SH SYNOPSIS
mbphotogrammetry [\fB\-\-verbose\fP \fB\-\-help\fP \fB\-\-threads=\fP\fInthreads\fP
\fB\-\-show\-images\fP \fB\-\-input=\fP\fIimagelist\fP \fB\-\-fov\-fudgefactor=\fP\fIfactor\fP
\fB\-\-navigation\-file=\fP\fIfile\fP \fB\-\-survey\-line\-file=\fP\fIfile\fP
\fB\-\-tide\-file=\fP\fIfile\fP \fB\-\-image\-quality\-file=\fP\fIfile\fP
\fB\-\-image\-quality\-threshold=\fP\fIvalue\fP
\fB\-\-image\-quality\-filter\-length=\fP\fIvalue\fP
\fB\-\-output=\fP\fIfileroot\fP \fB\-\-output\-number\-pairs=\fP\fIvalue\fP
\fB\-\-camera\-calibration\-file=\fP\fIfile\fP | \fB\-\-calibration\-file=\fP\fIfile\fP
\fB\-\-platform\-file=\fP\fIplatform.plf\fP \fB\-\-camera\-sensor=\fP\fIid\fP
\fB\-\-nav\-sensor=\fP\fIid\fP \fB\-\-sensordepth\-sensor=\fP\fIid\fP
\fB\-\-heading\-sensor=\fP\fIid\fP \fB\-\-altitude\-sensor=\fP\fIid\fP
\fB\-\-attitude\-sensor=\fP\fIid\fP
\fB\-\-altitude\-min=\fP\fIvalue\fP \fB\-\-altitude\-max=\fP\fIvalue\fP
\fB\-\-trim=\fP\fIvalue\fP \fB\-\-bin\-size=\fP\fIvalue\fP \fB\-\-bin\-filter=\fP\fIvalue\fP
\fB\-\-downsample=\fP\fIvalue\fP \fB\-\-algorithm=\fP\fIalgorithm\fP
\fB\-\-algorithm\-pre\-filter\-cap=\fP\fIvalue\fP
\fB\-\-algorithm\-sad\-window\-size=\fP\fIvalue\fP
\fB\-\-algorithm\-smoothing\-penalty\-1=\fP\fIvalue\fP
\fB\-\-algorithm\-smoothing\-penalty\-2=\fP\fIvalue\fP
\fB\-\-algorithm\-min\-disparity=\fP\fIvalue\fP
\fB\-\-algorithm\-number\-disparities=\fP\fIvalue\fP
\fB\-\-algorithm\-uniqueness\-ratio=\fP\fIvalue\fP
\fB\-\-algorithm\-speckle\-window\-size=\fP\fIvalue\fP
\fB\-\-algorithm\-speckle\-range=\fP\fIvalue\fP
\fB\-\-algorithm\-disp\-12\-max\-diff=\fP\fIvalue\fP
\fB\-\-algorithm\-texture\-threshold=\fP\fIvalue\fP]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBMbphotogrammetry\fP generates bathymetry soundings from navigated stereo
pairs of downlooking photographs taken from a submerged survey platform. For
each stereo pair listed in an input MB-System imagelist file, the program
computes a dense disparity map between the (optionally undistorted and
rectified) left and right images using one of OpenCV's block matching stereo
correspondence algorithms, then converts the resulting disparities into 3D
points using the stereo camera's calibrated geometry. These 3D points are
combined with the platform's navigation, heading, and attitude at the time
each stereo pair was taken (derived directly from the imagelist and,
optionally, an MB-System platform offset model and separate navigation and
tide files) to compute georeferenced soundings, which are binned and written
out as MB-System multibeam-format soundings (format 251, \fImb251\fP,
associated with the \fImbsys_stereopair\fP data structure).
.P
Three OpenCV stereo correspondence algorithms are supported: block matching
(\fBbm\fP), semi-global block matching (\fBsgbm\fP, the default), and its more
exhaustive variant (\fBhh\fP). Numerous options tune the chosen algorithm's
matching window, disparity range, smoothing penalties, and validity checks;
these correspond directly to the parameters of OpenCV's \fBStereoBM\fP and
\fBStereoSGBM\fP classes. Soundings whose stereo-derived altitude falls outside
the range set by \fB\-\-altitude\-min\fP and \fB\-\-altitude\-max\fP are rejected. Output
soundings can optionally be binned spatially, with each bin's disparity
resolved either by taking the mean or the median of the pixels falling in
that bin.
.P
Input images can be filtered by an externally computed per-image quality
metric (\fB\-\-image\-quality\-file\fP together with \fB\-\-image\-quality\-threshold\fP),
and processing can be parallelized across multiple stereo pairs at once with
\fB\-\-threads\fP. Output soundings are normally written to a single file named
from \fB\-\-output\fP with the suffix \fI.mb251\fP, but can instead be split into a
new output file every \fB\-\-output\-number\-pairs\fP stereo pairs, or split at the
waypoints of a survey line file supplied with \fB\-\-survey\-line\-file\fP.

