.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
This "help" flag causes the program to print out a description
of its operation and then exit immediately.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
The \fB\-\-verbose\fP option causes \fBmbphotogrammetry\fP to print out status and
debug messages. Using it more than once increases the verbosity level.
.TP
.B \-\-threads=\fInthreads\fP
.br
Sets the number of processing threads used to work through the stereo pairs
in the image list. The requested number of threads is limited to the number
of hardware threads available and to the MB-System maximum thread count. The
default is 1 thread.
.TP
.B \-\-show\-images
.br
Enables display of the images being processed (via OpenCV's image display
windows) as the program runs.
.TP
.B \-\-input=\fIimagelist\fP
.br
Sets the filename of the input MB-System imagelist file listing the stereo
image pairs, and their navigation, attitude, and camera settings, to be
processed. The default input filename is \fIimagelist.mb\-1\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-fov\-fudgefactor=\fIfactor\fP
.br
Sets a multiplicative fudge factor applied to the camera field of view
angles. The default value is 1.0 (no adjustment).
.TP
.B \-\-navigation\-file=\fIfile\fP
.br
Sets the filename of an ASCII navigation file used in place of, or to
supplement, navigation carried in the imagelist file.
.TP
.B \-\-survey\-line\-file=\fIfile\fP
.br
Sets the filename of a survey line/route file whose waypoint times are used
to split the output soundings into a separate \fI.mb251\fP output file at each
waypoint crossed.
.TP
.B \-\-tide\-file=\fIfile\fP
.br
Sets the filename of an ASCII tide file (time and tide height pairs) used to
apply a tidal correction to the computed soundings.
.TP
.B \-\-image\-quality\-file=\fIfile\fP
.br
Sets the filename of an ASCII file of time-stamped image quality values used
to filter out low quality stereo pairs.
.TP
.B \-\-image\-quality\-threshold=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Sets the minimum image quality value (in the range 0 to 1) required for a
stereo pair to be processed.
.TP
.B \-\-image\-quality\-filter\-length=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Sets a time filter length, in seconds, applied when interpolating image
quality values from the image quality file.
.TP
.B \-\-output=\fIfileroot\fP
.br
Sets the root name used to construct the output sounding file name(s). Unless
\fB\-\-survey\-line\-file\fP or \fB\-\-output\-number\-pairs\fP is used to split the output
into multiple files, all soundings are written to a single file named
\fIfileroot\fP\fB.mb251\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-output\-number\-pairs=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Splits the output soundings into a new file, named
\fIfileroot\fP\fB_\fP\fInnn\fP\fB.mb251\fP, every time \fIvalue\fP stereo pairs have been
written to the current output file. This option is ignored if
\fB\-\-survey\-line\-file\fP is also used.
.TP
.B \-\-camera\-calibration\-file=\fIfile\fP
.br
.TP
.B \-\-calibration\-file=\fIfile\fP
.br
These two equivalent options set the filename of an OpenCV YAML file
containing the intrinsic and extrinsic stereo camera calibration parameters
(camera matrices, distortion coefficients, and the rotation/translation
between the two cameras) used to undistort and rectify stereo pairs that are
not already rectified, and to convert stereo disparities into 3D coordinates.
.TP
.B \-\-platform\-file=\fIplatform.plf\fP
.br
Sets the filename of an MB-System platform definition file describing the
geometric offsets between the vehicle's navigation, attitude, and camera
sensors.
.TP
.B \-\-camera\-sensor=\fIcamera_sensor_id\fP
.br
Sets the platform sensor id number of the stereo camera used to look up the
camera's position and orientation offsets within the platform model.
.TP
.B \-\-nav\-sensor=\fInav_sensor_id\fP
.br
Overrides the platform model's navigation (position) source sensor id number.
.TP
.B \-\-sensordepth\-sensor=\fIsensordepth_sensor_id\fP
.br
Overrides the platform model's pressure/depth source sensor id number.
.TP
.B \-\-heading\-sensor=\fIheading_sensor_id\fP
.br
Overrides the platform model's heading source sensor id number.
.TP
.B \-\-altitude\-sensor=\fIaltitude_sensor_id\fP
.br
Sets the platform sensor id number used as the altitude source.
.TP
.B \-\-attitude\-sensor=\fIattitude_sensor_id\fP
.br
Overrides the platform model's roll/pitch and heave source sensor id number.
.TP
.B \-\-altitude\-min=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Sets the minimum acceptable stereo-derived altitude, in meters, for a
sounding to be retained. The default is 1.0 meter.
.TP
.B \-\-altitude\-max=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Sets the maximum acceptable stereo-derived altitude, in meters, for a
sounding to be retained. The default is 5.0 meters.
.TP
.B \-\-trim=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Sets a pixel trim margin excluded around the edges of each stereo image before
computing disparity. The default is 0.0 (no trim).
.TP
.B \-\-bin\-size=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Sets the size, in pixels, of the spatial bins used to combine disparity
values before generating output soundings. The default is 1 (no binning).
.TP
.B \-\-bin\-filter=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Selects how disparity values are combined within each spatial bin: \fBmean\fP
(or \fB0\fP) averages the values in the bin, while \fBmedian\fP (or \fB1\fP) takes
the median value. The default is \fBmean\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-downsample=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Sets a downsampling factor applied to the stereo images before disparity
matching. The default is 1 (no downsampling).
.TP
.B \-\-algorithm=\fIalgorithm\fP
.br
Selects the OpenCV stereo correspondence algorithm used to compute
disparities. Valid values are \fBbm\fP (block matching), \fBsgbm\fP (semi-global
block matching, the default), and \fBhh\fP (a more exhaustive variant of
semi-global block matching).
.TP
.B \-\-algorithm\-pre\-filter\-cap=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Sets the truncation value for prefiltered image pixels used by the stereo
correspondence algorithm. The default is 4.
.TP
.B \-\-algorithm\-sad\-window\-size=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Sets the matched block (sum of absolute differences window) size used by the
stereo correspondence algorithm. The default is 5.
.TP
.B \-\-algorithm\-smoothing\-penalty\-1=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Sets the first smoothness penalty parameter (P1) controlling disparity
change of one pixel between neighboring pixels, used by the semi-global block
matching algorithms. The default is 600.
.TP
.B \-\-algorithm\-smoothing\-penalty\-2=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Sets the second smoothness penalty parameter (P2) controlling larger
disparity changes between neighboring pixels, used by the semi-global block
matching algorithms. The default is 2400.
.TP
.B \-\-algorithm\-min\-disparity=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Sets the minimum possible disparity value used by the stereo correspondence
algorithm. The default is -64.
.TP
.B \-\-algorithm\-number\-disparities=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Sets the number of disparity values searched by the stereo correspondence
algorithm (the disparity search range). The default is 192.
.TP
.B \-\-algorithm\-uniqueness\-ratio=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Sets the margin, in percent, by which the best matching disparity cost must
beat the next best value for a match to be considered valid. The default is 1.
.TP
.B \-\-algorithm\-speckle\-window\-size=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Sets the maximum size of smooth disparity regions considered noise speckles
and invalidated by the stereo correspondence algorithm's postfiltering. The
default is 150.
.TP
.B \-\-algorithm\-speckle\-range=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Sets the maximum disparity variation within a connected component considered
during speckle postfiltering. The default is 2.
.TP
.B \-\-algorithm\-disp\-12\-max\-diff=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Sets the maximum allowed difference, in integer pixel units, between the
left-to-right and right-to-left disparity checks. The default is 10.
.TP
.B \-\-algorithm\-texture\-threshold=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Sets a texture threshold value used to reject matches in low-texture image
regions. The default is 10.

